@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Passkey account UI
+
+This repository is a static site and contains no session service, credential database, or WebAuthn registration backend. The account screen therefore defaults to an explicitly labeled local preview. Preview changes persist in browser storage, and preview IDs are never sent to a browser authenticator. No actual passkey authentication or registration is simulated.
+
+The original homepage links to the new screen at `/account/` (`account/index.html`). To connect the screen, change `data-account-mode="preview"` to `data-account-mode="connected"` in that file and implement the same-origin API below. Connected mode never falls back to demo data on an authentication or service failure.
+
+## API contract
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: return the signed-in customer's complete credential snapshot.
+- `PUT /api/account/passkeys/:id`: accept JSON `{ "name": "My laptop" }`, persist the trimmed nickname (1–60 characters), then return the complete updated snapshot.
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: delete the credential, then return the complete remaining snapshot, including an empty array when appropriate.
+
+Every successful response must have `Content-Type: application/json` and this shape:
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "your-registration-rp.example",
+  "userId": "dXNlci0x",
+  "credentials": [
+    {
+      "id": "Y3JlZGVudGlhbC0x",
+      "name": "My laptop",
+      "aaguid": "08987058-cadc-4b81-b6e1-30de50dcbe96",
+      "registeredAt": 1789171200000,
+      "lastUsedAt": null
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Use the RP ID originally used in registration, not the page's hostname. `userId` is the WebAuthn user handle, encoded as unpadded Base64URL; credential IDs use the same encoding. Dates are persisted epoch milliseconds, not preformatted strings. Never expose public keys, challenges, or other users' records here.
+
+The backend must authenticate every request using the existing customer session, derive ownership from that session, enforce ownership on each mutation, validate request names, apply same-origin/CSRF protections, and disable response caching. Use 401/403 for expired or unauthorized sessions, 404 for credentials the customer cannot access, and a non-2xx response for failed changes. Enforce any policy preventing deletion of the last available authentication method on the backend; the UI also warns before deleting the last passkey. Serialize mutations per customer or use transactional snapshots so the returned list is complete and current.
+
+After initial load and each successful deletion, connected mode feature-detects `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` and shares the complete accepted list with the browser. Unsupported browsers and passive synchronization failures do not undo successful server changes, and the UI explains manual cleanup. A passkey nickname is an account-local label; it must not invoke `signalCurrentUserDetails`, which is for account profile names, not credential labels.
+
+The AAGUID registry subset only supplies display hints and uses a generic fallback for unknown or zero AAGUIDs. It is never used for security decisions. Source: https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids
+
+Run the focused, server-free checks with `node --test tests/*.test.mjs` and `node --check account.mjs`. No build step is needed for this static site.
